# 🐳 Keeps `docker build`'s context to what the Rust build actually reads.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` sends the whole working tree — on this machine
# that includes a `target/` in the tens of gigabytes, gitignored so it never
# reaches CI, but very real for anyone running `docker build` locally from a
# repo they have been building in. A slow, disk-hungry `docker build` is
# exactly the kind of friction that makes people stop trusting the Dockerfile,
# which is the thing this repo already paid for once today.

.git
/target
**/target

# 📄 Evidence and planning material the binary never reads.
benchmarks/results
docs

# 🌐 The doc site's own dependency tree, once it has one (docs/SITE.md).
site/node_modules

.DS_Store
